---
title: Patterns
description: Line work, marks, light and texture for backgrounds — seventeen of them, all pure CSS, all drawn from tokens so they follow dark mode. For the space behind a hero, an empty cell, a placeholder.
eyebrow: Foundation
source: src/utilities/patterns.css
---
<h2>How they work</h2>
<p>Each is a utility that sets <code>background-image</code> and nothing else, so it combines with any <code>bg-*</code> colour and takes variants (<code>md:im-bg-grid</code>). Three knobs apply to all of them:</p>
<div class="im-table-scroll">
<table>
	<thead><tr><th>Variable</th><th></th></tr></thead>
	<tbody>
		<tr><td><code>--im-pattern-size</code></td><td>The pitch — the distance between repeats.</td></tr>
		<tr><td><code>--im-pattern-color</code></td><td>The ink. Defaults to <code>--im-line</code> (or <code>--im-faint</code> for marks).</td></tr>
		<tr><td><code>--im-pattern-weight</code></td><td>Line thickness, where there are lines. 1px.</td></tr>
	</tbody>
</table>
</div>

<h2>Lines</h2>
{{#example}}
<div class="im-grid-auto" style="--im-grid-min: 10rem; --im-grid-gap: .75rem">
	<div class="pattern-tile im-bg-grid">im-bg-grid</div>
	<div class="pattern-tile im-bg-blueprint">im-bg-blueprint</div>
	<div class="pattern-tile im-bg-rules">im-bg-rules</div>
	<div class="pattern-tile im-bg-columns">im-bg-columns</div>
	<div class="pattern-tile im-bg-lines">im-bg-lines</div>
	<div class="pattern-tile im-bg-diamond">im-bg-diamond</div>
	<div class="pattern-tile im-bg-isometric">im-bg-isometric</div>
</div>
{{/example}}

<h2>Marks</h2>
{{#example}}
<div class="im-grid-auto" style="--im-grid-min: 10rem; --im-grid-gap: .75rem">
	<div class="pattern-tile im-bg-dots">im-bg-dots</div>
	<div class="pattern-tile im-bg-cross">im-bg-cross</div>
	<div class="pattern-tile im-bg-checker">im-bg-checker</div>
	<div class="pattern-tile im-bg-rings">im-bg-rings</div>
	<div class="pattern-tile im-bg-zigzag">im-bg-zigzag</div>
	<div class="pattern-tile im-bg-stripes">im-bg-stripes</div>
</div>
{{/example}}

<p><code>im-bg-cross</code> is the one exception to the colour knob: a <code>+</code> cannot be drawn with gradients, so it is an inline SVG tile in a fixed mid-grey that reads on light and dark alike. <code>--im-pattern-size</code> still applies.</p>

<h2>Light &amp; texture</h2>
{{#example}}
<div class="im-grid-auto" style="--im-grid-min: 12rem; --im-grid-gap: .75rem">
	<div class="pattern-tile im-bg-glow">im-bg-glow</div>
	<div class="pattern-tile im-bg-glow" style="--im-pattern-at: 100% 100%; --im-pattern-color: var(--im-info)">glow · placed, recoloured</div>
	<div class="pattern-tile im-bg-mesh">im-bg-mesh</div>
	<div class="pattern-tile im-bg-noise bg-surface">im-bg-noise on bg-surface</div>
</div>
{{/example}}
<p><code>im-bg-glow</code> is placed with <code>--im-pattern-at</code> (any <code>background-position</code>). <code>im-bg-noise</code> is one inline SVG turbulence — no request — and is meant to sit over a colour.</p>

<h2>Tuning</h2>
{{#example}}
<div class="im-grid-auto" style="--im-grid-min: 10rem; --im-grid-gap: .75rem">
	<div class="pattern-tile im-bg-grid" style="--im-pattern-size: 1rem">size 1rem</div>
	<div class="pattern-tile im-bg-grid" style="--im-pattern-color: var(--im-accent)">accent ink</div>
	<div class="pattern-tile im-bg-lines" style="--im-pattern-weight: 3px; --im-pattern-size: 1rem">weight 3px</div>
	<div class="pattern-tile im-bg-dots" style="--im-pattern-size: .625rem; --im-pattern-color: var(--im-ink)">dense, ink</div>
	<div class="pattern-tile im-bg-rings" style="--im-pattern-at: 0% 100%; --im-pattern-size: 1rem">rings from a corner</div>
	<div class="pattern-tile im-bg-stripes" style="--im-pattern-color: var(--im-warning-tint)">warning stripes</div>
</div>
{{/example}}

<h2>Fading one out</h2>
<p>A pattern at full strength behind text is noise. Fade it with a mask — and put the pattern on its <strong>own layer</strong>, because a mask fades everything inside the element it is on.</p>
{{#example}}
<div class="im-grid-auto" style="--im-grid-min: 10rem; --im-grid-gap: .75rem">
	<div class="pattern-tile im-bg-grid im-fade-b">im-fade-b</div>
	<div class="pattern-tile im-bg-grid im-fade-t">im-fade-t</div>
	<div class="pattern-tile im-bg-grid im-fade-x">im-fade-x</div>
	<div class="pattern-tile im-bg-grid im-fade-radial">im-fade-radial</div>
	<div class="pattern-tile im-bg-grid im-fade-corner">im-fade-corner</div>
</div>
{{/example}}
{{#example flush=true title="Layered: blueprint faded from a corner, a glow, and grain — behind real content"}}
<div class="relative isolate overflow-hidden px-8 py-14">
	<div class="im-bg-blueprint im-fade-corner absolute inset-0 -z-10" aria-hidden="true"></div>
	<div class="im-bg-glow absolute inset-0 -z-10" style="--im-pattern-at: 100% 0%" aria-hidden="true"></div>
	<div class="im-bg-noise absolute inset-0 -z-10 opacity-40" aria-hidden="true"></div>
	<p class="im-caption" data-index="→">Patterns, layered</p>
	<h3 class="text-h1 mt-3" style="max-width: 18ch">Each on its own layer, all behind the words.</h3>
	<div class="im-cluster mt-5"><a class="im-btn im-btn-primary" href="#fading-one-out">Start</a><a class="im-btn" href="#fading-one-out">Docs</a></div>
</div>
{{/example}}

<h2>Drifting</h2>
<p><code>im-bg-drift</code> pans a repeating pattern by exactly one pitch, forever, so the loop has no seam. <code>--im-pattern-speed</code> (40s). It stops under reduced motion.</p>
{{#example}}
<div class="im-grid-auto" style="--im-grid-min: 12rem; --im-grid-gap: .75rem">
	<div class="pattern-tile im-bg-grid im-bg-drift" style="--im-pattern-speed: 12s">grid, drifting</div>
	<div class="pattern-tile im-bg-dots im-bg-drift" style="--im-pattern-size: 1.25rem; --im-pattern-speed: 8s">dots, drifting</div>
</div>
{{/example}}

<h2>Using them well</h2>
<ul>
	<li><strong>One pattern per view</strong>, two at most if one is light or grain.</li>
	<li><strong>Behind content, never behind body text at full strength.</strong> Fade it, or keep it to the margins.</li>
	<li><strong>Empty space is a fine place for one</strong> — a filler cell in a grid, an image placeholder, a "nothing here yet" state.</li>
	<li>They are decoration: mark the layer <code>aria-hidden="true"</code>.</li>
</ul>


<h2>More line work, and variations</h2>
<p><code>im-bg-hatch</code> · <code>im-bg-lattice</code> · <code>im-bg-radar</code> · <code>im-bg-waves</code> · <code>im-bg-bricks</code> · <code>im-bg-plus</code>. Then a variation on any of them: <code>im-bg-fade-r</code>, <code>im-bg-fade-b</code>, <code>im-bg-corner</code> mask it to one edge or corner; <code>im-bg-dense</code> / <code>im-bg-loose</code> change the pitch; <code>im-bg-accent</code> inks it in the accent. A pattern that fills a panel is wallpaper; one that fades is a mark.</p>
{{#example}}
<div class="im-grid-auto" style="--im-grid-min: 9rem; --im-grid-gap: .75rem">
	<div class="im-bg-hatch" style="aspect-ratio: 1; border-radius: var(--im-radius-lg)"></div>
	<div class="im-bg-lattice" style="aspect-ratio: 1; border-radius: var(--im-radius-lg)"></div>
	<div class="im-bg-radar" style="aspect-ratio: 1; border-radius: var(--im-radius-lg)"></div>
	<div class="im-bg-waves" style="aspect-ratio: 1; border-radius: var(--im-radius-lg)"></div>
	<div class="im-bg-bricks" style="aspect-ratio: 1; border-radius: var(--im-radius-lg)"></div>
	<div class="im-bg-plus" style="aspect-ratio: 1; border-radius: var(--im-radius-lg)"></div>
	<div class="im-bg-grid im-bg-fade-r im-bg-accent" style="aspect-ratio: 1; border-radius: var(--im-radius-lg)"></div>
	<div class="im-bg-dots im-bg-corner im-bg-dense" style="aspect-ratio: 1; border-radius: var(--im-radius-lg)"></div>
</div>
{{/example}}
